# No submodules. This file exists for Claude Code's Linux sandbox, which
# protects .gitmodules from writes and, when the file is absent, masks the
# path with a placeholder that exists but cannot be opened. Nix's git fetcher
# checks for .gitmodules before evaluating a flake from a checkout and fails
# on that placeholder. A real file is bound read-only instead, and reads as
# "no submodules".
